  "drivers": "The S&P 500 is up 0.7% and touched 7,835.09, a new high above its August record, as Treasury yields and oil ease. The 10-year yield slipped to about 5.29% from Monday's 2002-era peak, and WTI fell 1.6% to near $88. Power and nuclear stocks are rallying after Constellation Energy agreed to supply Google with 890 MW of new nuclear capacity, and AI-chip names are firm after Marvell raised its long-term revenue targets. Biotech is the weak spot (XBI −3.5%) as Spyre and Vaxcyte sell new shares, and small caps are lagging. August's trade deficit widened to $105.6B, wider than the $102.0B expected, on a 4.3% jump in imports.",
